.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man1/dumpkeys.1, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt DUMPKEYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dumpkeys
.Nd print console keyboard maps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h i l n V
.Op Fl C Ar console
.Op Fl c Ar charset
.Op Fl S Ar shape
.Op Fl Fl keys-only
.Op Fl Fl funcs-only
.Op Fl Fl compose-only
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the console's key definitions, function strings and compose table
in the text format read by
.Xr loadkeys 1 .
With no options it prints all three.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl C Ar console
Read this console device.
.It Fl c Ar charset
Interpret action codes in the named character set.
.It Fl i
Print a summary of the kernel's keyboard capabilities.
.It Fl l
List the known action names and values.
Repeated, include their synonyms.
.It Fl n
Print action values numerically.
.It Fl S Ar shape
Select output shape 2 (compact), 4 (one line per keycode),
8 (one line per modifier and keycode), or 16 (stop at the first hole).
.It Fl Fl keys-only
Print only key bindings.
.It Fl Fl funcs-only
Print only function strings.
.It Fl Fl compose-only
Print only compose definitions.
.It Fl h
Print help without opening the console.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loadkeys 1 ,
.Xr kbd_mode 1
